Phase-001 is done and green. Summary of what happened:

## Finding re-verified (and it was worse than recorded)

`cargo run --bin rb -- run wrong.rb` → `Error: ParserError: Unexpected token Expect`. `Expr::Expect` was **never constructed anywhere in `src/parser.rs`** — so `expect …` didn't even parse. The phase's premise is sound.

## What changed (`redblue/`, +604 −46)

- **`src/parser.rs`** — `expect <expr> to be|contain <expr>` now parses into `Expr::Expect`; new `ExpectMatcher`. `be`/`contain` are matched as **identifiers, not new tokens**, so neither word becomes reserved.
- **`src/testing/harness.rs`** — runs every top-level `test "name" … end`, walks the body in order, and evaluates each `expect` through `testing::assertions`. A mismatch is an assertion failure with expected/actual, not a bare runtime error.
- **`src/vm.rs`** — `Expr::Expect` honours the matcher; `evaluate_expression` / `execute_statements` / `flush_output` exposed so the harness can interleave assertions without the VM parsing anything.
- **`src/testing/assertions.rs`**, **`src/value.rs`** — `assert_value_contains`, `Value::contains_item`.
- **`src/lib.rs`** — `rb test <file>` now prints a summary and exits 1 on failure, like the no-path branch.

## Evidence the tests can fail

Temporarily made `check_expectation` discard its result → **11 of the 25 new tests went red**, including `test_wrong_expectation_fails_the_test`. Reverted. Also `rb test` on `expect 1 to be 2` → `FAILED edge_wrong_expectation: Values not equal: Number(2.0) vs Number(1.0)`, exit 1.

`cargo fmt --check` pass · `cargo clippy -D warnings` pass · `cargo test --all-targets` **35 passed, 0 failed** · 6/6 examples run · all 11 edge-matrix rows covered.

## One thing I could not fix, and did not fake

`./rbops/verify.sh phase-001` as CI invokes it **FAILS with 2 checks** — `phase-001 is NOT declared in rbops/phases.json` and `example fails: modules/MathUtils.rb`. One root cause, not my change: `verify.sh:17,24` default `PHASES`/`BASELINE` to *relative* paths and `verify.sh:27` `cd`s into `redblue/` before reading them, and nothing ever copies `rbops/` into the cloned `redblue/`. **Every phase will fail this way, including one that changes nothing.**

Proof it is the wiring: pointing the two env vars `verify.sh` already supports at the real files gives **VERIFY PASS** (25 PASS, 1 baselined WARN, 0 FAIL).

I did not touch `rbops/` (hard rule 1), and creating `redblue/rbops/phases.json` would trip the gate's own forbidden-path scan. Full diagnosis, a one-line-each fix suggestion, and six other findings (MathUtils, out-of-range indexing that returns a value instead of raising, `f64` precision at 2^53, an **inverted** `AssertThat::contains`, a duplicate `TestAssertionError` in `runner.rs`, phase-002's discovery bug) are in `phases/phase-001/FINDINGS.md`. `REPORT.md` and `FINDINGS.md` are written to both `redblue/phases/phase-001/` (canonical, pushed to the redblue repo) and `phases/phase-001/` (what the reviewer reads).
